<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<title>LithoKraft — Full Test (GL / WebGL2 path)</title>
<style>
  body { background:#0A0A12; color:#E8E4F8; font-family: system-ui, sans-serif;
         display:flex; flex-direction:column; align-items:center; padding:24px; margin:0; }
  h1 { color:#A970FF; font-size:20px; margin:0 0 4px; }
  p.sub { color:#9a93b8; margin:0 0 12px; font-size:13px; max-width:900px; text-align:center; }
  .ab { font:13px ui-monospace, monospace; margin-bottom:12px; }
  .ab a { color:#A970FF; } .ab b { color:#FF6F00; }
  canvas { width:960px; height:540px; background:#000;
           border:1px solid #2c2748; border-radius:6px; }
  #status { margin-top:12px; font:13px ui-monospace, monospace; color:#FF6F00; }
  #log { margin-top:8px; width:960px; max-height:260px; overflow:auto; white-space:pre-wrap;
         font:11px ui-monospace, monospace; color:#b9b3d6; background:#0d0d18;
         border:1px solid #2c2748; border-radius:6px; padding:8px; box-sizing:border-box; }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<h1>LITHOKRAFT &mdash; FULL TEST</h1>
<p class="sub">The full engine + game in WebAssembly. This page boots the
<b>GL33 renderer on WebGL2</b> (shaders: the pack carries GLSL ES 3.00
translations; the renderer logs per-shader verdicts; chunk meshes run with
<code>--gl-arena off</code> because WebGL2 has no base-vertex draw &mdash;
same meshes and pixels, per-mesh VAOs instead of one arena). Same build,
same world seed, same bench as the software page.</p>
<div class="ab">A/B present path: <a href="index.html">&larr; SOFTWARE</a> &nbsp;|&nbsp; <b>GL (WebGL2)</b></div>
<canvas id="canvas" width="1280" height="720" oncontextmenu="event.preventDefault()"></canvas>
<div id="status">booting&hellip;</div>
<div id="log"></div>
<script>
  // Module (with print + boot arguments) is defined BEFORE LithoKraft.js
  // loads — the runtime reads its callbacks at init completion, so a
  // Module assigned afterwards races the runtime (web-spike lesson #8).
  const logEl = document.getElementById('log');
  const statusEl = document.getElementById('status');
  function toLog(s) { logEl.textContent += s + '\n'; logEl.scrollTop = logEl.scrollHeight; }
  var Module = {
    canvas: document.getElementById('canvas'),
    arguments: ['--renderer', 'gl33', '--gl-arena', 'off',
                '--bench', '4', '--bench-path', 'orbit',
                '--seed', '20261019',
                '--scripts', 'exe', '--mute',
                '--ui-shot', '/ui-gl.png',
                '--bench-json', '/bench-gl.json'],
    print: (s) => toLog(s),
    printErr: (s) => toLog('ERR: ' + s),
    onExit: (code) => { statusEl.textContent = 'run finished (exit ' + code + ') — bench summary in the log above'; },
    setStatus: (s) => { if (s) statusEl.textContent = s; },
  };
  window.addEventListener('error', (e) => { statusEl.textContent = 'error: ' + e.message; });
</script>
<script src="LithoKraft.js"></script>
</body>
</html>
